--- Rosetta Code: Copy stdin to stdout
--- https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Copy_stdin_to_stdout
--- Read standard input a line at a time until it ends (input[] at the end of
--- the input is an error value) and write each line back out. Run it as
---     crow run copy_stdin_to_stdout.co < some.txt
--- A line's ending is written as one line feed; on Unix,
--- write['/dev/stdout', read['/dev/stdin']] copies the bytes exactly instead.

line = input[]
while line.ok
    log[line]
    line = input[]
